{
  "_comment": "The herdr the suite is judged against, reproduced rather than installed - the same arrangement as deps/ghostty.pin. ./dev downloads this platform's asset into deps/herdr/<version>/ once, verifies it against the checksum here, and hands that path to every daemon-backed test. Nothing reads the developer's PATH, so the herdr you run for your own work is free to be any version. Checksums are ours rather than upstream's: herdr publishes no manifest, and what belongs in a pin is the exact bytes this corpus was recorded against. Re-pinning means changing the version, re-downloading, re-recording the corpus with tools/herdr-probe/probe, and reading what moved.",
  "version": "0.8.0",
